    <meta property="og:url" content="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10853-026-13462-9"/>
    <meta property="og:type" content="article"/>
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="SpringerLink"/>
    <meta property="og:title" content="Physical, mechanical and electrochemical performance of nanostructured TiO2 surface on titanium developed by anodization - Journal of Materials Science"/>
    <meta property="og:description" content="This study investigates the formation and characterization of self&#8211;organized TiO2 coatings on titanium foil via anodization to enhance surface&#8211;dependent mechanical and electrochemical properties for biomedical applications. Anodization was performed in an ethylene glycol-based organic electrolyte containing 0.4 wt.% NH4F at ambient temperature, with applied voltages ranging from 15 to 60 V and durations from 0.5 to 9 h. The resulting nanostructured TiO2 coatings exhibited morphology and dimensions dependent on process parameters. TiO2-coated surfaces showed significantly reduced nano&#8211;hardness (2.43 GPa for anodized at 45 V) compared to the untreated Ti foil (3.4 GPa). The TiO2 nanofilm exhibited hydrophilic behaviour, with a contact angle of 0&#176; at 60 V. Corrosion resistance and bioactivity were notably improved following anodization. These findings suggest that optimizing anodization parameters can effectively tailor surface properties, making them suitable for biomedical implant applications and corrosion&#8211;resistant coatings. Graphical abstract"/>
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs10853-026-13462-9/MediaObjects/10853_2026_13462_Figa_HTML.png"/>
    

        

